To transfer information from a clicked button (or cell) to your `.js` file, you typically use an event listener in JavaScript. The click event handler receives an event object, which allows you to access properties of the clicked element.

Basic event listener syntax:
```js
element.addEventListener('click', function(event) {
  // event.target gives the clicked element
});
```

Alternatively, in HTML, you can use the `onclick` attribute:
```html
<button onclick="functionName(this)">Click me</button>
```
In this case, `this` refers to the clicked element, which your JavaScript function can use.

